module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**bare name resolved by proximity, standing in for resolution** (the reference-edge reader in `v1_compiler.cli_run` `entry_resolve` binds a bare name in an IMPORT-LESS file by 'proximity disambiguation' -- the longest shared module-path prefix with a pool declarer -- yielding a UniqueBare or AmbiguousBare edge. A heuristic standing where lexical resolution (locals plus imports) is the authority; DESIGN §4: in a closed system a heuristic is never necessary.)",

    "INVALID STATE: a dependency edge from a module to a declarer it does not lexically bind. The edge widens closures and affected-set selection and can name a homonym the source never meant, silently, with no refusal.",

    "SPECIMEN (gunbc#13526, open when this row was written): a supplied fixture declaring a homonym `Present` beside `std.optional { Present }` produced an edge from an importer of `std.optional` to the homonym's module while the reader still resolved by proximity. #13526 closed the arm for import-BEARING files (bare names there are lexically bound, only qualified chains become edges) and kept the proximity tier for import-less files only.",

    "RUNG: BELOW THE FLOOR for the surviving import-less path -- silent wrongness, which is outside the ladder (§4b) and forbidden outright, not a mitigation rung. A bare name in an import-less file whose declarer the proximity rule picks wrongly yields an edge with no refusal, and the UniqueBare/AmbiguousBare typing does not make that visible to the consumer that reads the edge. For import-BEARING files the class is closed: #13526 removed the tier there (bare names are lexically bound), which is the only executed wall. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed, at the boundary SOURCE -> ACCEPTED GRAPH: no Accepted graph contains a proximity-guessed edge. Bare names are decidable by lexical resolution, so a bare name either binds lexically or the source is refused before any graph is accepted; a runtime typed refusal at the reader alone would be mitigation and does not establish this rung. No grounding is missing.",

    "EVIDENCE, STATED PLAINLY: there is NO executing evidence for the wrong-edge RED on the import-less path. The homonym RED in the open #13526 covers import-bearing files, where the tier no longer runs. The only executed control on the surviving path is a unit control added by the open gunbc#13526 (an import-less file resolving a bare name to a single pool declarer), which shows the proximity tier is LIVE for an import-less file resolving a bare name to a single pool declarer; it is not a discriminating RED for a wrong edge, so it does not establish a rung. A supplied-fixture RED (an import-less file whose bare name has a homonym, asserting the wrong proximity edge) is the missing evidence.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: bare names resolve lexically (locals plus imports) or the source is refused, so no Accepted graph carries a proximity-ranked edge; the proximity tier is deleted. The trigger is satisfied only by IMPORT-LESS evidence: (1) a wrong-edge RED on the import-less path -- a supplied-fixture import-less file whose bare name has a pool homonym must get NO proximity edge (or a refusal) -- and (2) a valid-binding positive control, an import-less file whose bare name is lexically bound and keeps its edge. An import-bearing RED does not count: it passes while its import-less companion keeps the guessed edge. Both stay enrolled as permanent controls.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a reader or resolver that ranks candidate declarers by path similarity, shared prefix or 'closest' instead of refusing; an edge whose only justification is that one pool declarer exists.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
